header='''# Selected social B02 original/target comparison

Ten complete headless compositions and thin shared-UI definitions are delivered for the ten immutable selected B02 paths. This is author/coordinator evidence; required independent Argon/high approval remains quota-blocked by8194e842 and was neither retried nor substituted. Parent owns all global ledger/count/acceptance decisions and final integration. Issue[21](https://github.com/dweigend/city-library/issues/21), draftPR[22](https://github.com/dweigend/city-library/pull/22), stacked on rootPR[4](https://github.com/dweigend/city-library/pull/4).

## Identity, contracts and execution basis

[Exact source manifest](selected-social-sources.json) pins fresh served bytes, source URLs, SHA-256/bytes and Galapagos90be931773fcf499049247a8aaa1aecbe003654c blob identity. All reconcile to immutable Web inventory and existing research archives; desktop membership is not used. Each experiment retains full source.nlogox/Info and NOTICE attribution/license (CC BY-NC-SA3.0). [Full audit](selected-social-source-audit.md) retains every widget/default/topology/procedure/plot/action; [binding interpretation](selected-social-contract.md) specifies rules, phase barriers, live/setup fields, terminal behavior and public actions. [First-five](selected-social-first-runtime.md) and [last-five](selected-social-last-runtime.md) reports detail public observations and reuse. No shared capability gap or generic private kernel was introduced.

Five asserted public scripts and hashes froze at a4afc4f before scoped runtime delegation to two disjoint five-model workers. All five remain byte-identical. Runtime equations use public City Library APIs; domain state remains canonical Agent/World/Grid/Graph or source-specific urn arrays. UI changes state through public actions only. The branch does not mutate shared src/index/UI/config/scripts, research, ledger, PLAN, README, approved diagram or another batch.

Actual T3 server Chromium156/Linux executed every original and target. Original default captures use native unseeded initialization; target captures use seed1. Native preset/intervention seeds are explicitly recorded. NetLogo MT and public Mulberry are different; no cross-RNG trajectory, statistical equivalence or empirical validation is claimed. Per-model JSON records actual ticks/reporters, literal native commands, source controls and errors. Separate loaded-public-model probes are executed in the same actual target browser; they are explicitly separate from the host-mounted instance. Host behavior is observed through its rendered monitors/actions.

For each original, SHA-256 is computed from actual UTF-8 `session.nlogoSource.nlogo`. The native session has no `nlogoSourceSHA` property. A discovery hash of String(object) was discarded and is not source evidence. All ten actual session hashes equal pinned files. Final target `ui.sourceMarker`, loaded model chunk SHA, shared chunk SHA and build version are in each target JSON and reconciled with [final served chunks](selected-social-evidence/final-served-chunks.json). [Runtime hashes](selected-social-evidence/runtime-SHA256SUMS) pin final model/UI, originals/notices and current unchanged core/shared renderer sources.

## Browser and design protocol

Original native Setup, single step where available (otherwise command-center GO), Run/Pause and Setup-as-reset were executed; source-specific controls/actions are separately recorded. All target Setup,1-step, progressing steps, Run/Pause, stable paused state, current live value into Setup, Model info and relevant actions passed. There is no separate Reset button in the shared host: Setup is the tested reset/reinitialization action. Every target has no duplicate setup/live field. Piaget randomized strategy may legitimately overwrite the selected strategy during Setup while randomization is enabled; the disabled-randomization test confirms exact control retention.

Desktop CSS viewport1440x1100 and mobile390x844, light/dark, were captured. T3 writes reduced desktop PNG1280x978 and mobile PNG780x1688; reported CSS dimensions are not confused with raster dimensions. Each model has paired original/target setup+progress, plus desktop-dark/mobile-light/mobile-dark. Final PNGs were visually inspected; controls wrap, scientific views/plots remain readable, mobile document width is390 without horizontal overflow, and keyboard Tab from Setup reaches Run with visible2px focus. Inspector and information disclosures were exercised where relevant. Existing shared semantic controls and chart alternatives remain; no new icon/style system was added. frontend-design and current Vercel web-design-guidelines were applied; this is not an accessibility certification.

Before capture, `getImageData` readback was applied to2D canvases and raster statistics retained. This is the documented raster-capture workaround, not a renderer fix. It does not close any parent renderer issue. Final page error/rejection hooks and scoped console warn/error instrumentation after mount/before Setup+step recorded no messages for all ten; pre-hook navigation-console output is not claimed captured. [Diagnostics](selected-social-evidence/final-diagnostics.json).

Author visual findings were fixed and rechecked: unscaled Consumer/Language projections, unsupported Cytoscape HSL syntax, low-contrast grammar colors, police hidden by jailed co-location, rightmost Party count clipping, and Piaget run restart. Consumer's superseded unscaled PNG/JSON and Language's superseded JSON remain explicitly historical. A same-URL T3 reuse retained an earlier Language module; final capture used a unique query and actual RGB/chunk reconciliation. A manual redraw call with missing arguments failed and was discarded; a Next run query initially raced mounting and was retried after waiting. These tool/capture failures do not establish target passes.

## Executed shell evidence

- `bun run typecheck`: all four TypeScript projects passed repeatedly, including after the final UI wording change.
- `bun test tests/selected-social-first.test.ts tests/selected-social-last.test.ts`:23 tests,4521 assertions,0 failures; [final focused log](selected-social-evidence/focused-tests.log).
- All five frozen selected-social scripts passed individually and together; [log](selected-social-evidence/frozen-examples.log), [immutable hashes](selected-social-example-SHA256SUMS).
- `bun run check`: final runtime392 tests/38849 assertions across45 files; all140 currently registered examples, library build and packed Bun/Node ESM/ambient-free TypeScript consumer passed. [Final log](selected-social-evidence/final-check.log). The subsequent UI-only diagnostic wording change passed typecheck and its repeated full browser flow. Parent will register the new phase globally; no shared scripts change is included here.
- `python docs/development/selected-social-verify.py`: ten exact sources/identities, five frozen scripts, ten paired browser records,70 final PNGs, current loaded/served chunk reconciliation and exclusive owned diff passed.

Initial missing Bun type definitions were resolved with an ignored environment-only symlink to the already installed pinned dependency tree. No dependency/configuration or lockfile changes were made. No custom lint command exists. Package consumer checks operate in temporary directories; no package was published.

'''
